    "done_when": "In imas_ambix/data/cocos_convention.py, _differential_flux_loop_targets finds the magnetics description store by the catalogue's declared magnetics system rather than by catalog.maps[0]. When it cannot read the store it raises, instead of returning an empty set that would admit every proven rule as an absolute loop. New tests in tests/data/test_cocos_convention.py pin both: a catalogue whose first map is not magnetics still resolves the store, and a missing store raises. The fragment answers the review's four findings. (1) The 12-27 corpus-validated split is declined as the lead's locked median rule (decision vacuum-verdict-rule), whose result the loop-reference RCA states. The fragment checks whether each loop rule's evidence string records its per-shot outliers, as that decision requires, and lists any that do not as a follow-on for a later maps edit, writing nothing under maps/. (2) The fail-closed selector. (3) A complete gate. (4) The inventory failure, already fixed on main and included in this base. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), with IMAS_ALAMBIC_MAP_PATH unset and the worktree's maps a symlink to the main checkout's maps/, run in the foreground with a time bound and capture once, to a log in the run directory (never /tmp) whose first lines give the head revision and command and whose last line is EXIT=: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/data/test_jt60sa_signal_maps.py tests/data/test_jt60sa_unit_audit.py tests/data/test_jt60sa_machine_map.py tests/gs/test_operator_differential_loops.py tests/data/test_cocos_convention.py. It exits 0. scripts/jt60sa_sign_cohort.py exits 0 still reporting COCOS (1, 2, 11, 12) over loop 7 alone, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. Write the manifest before any long wait. A landing fragment is written to the fragment path.",
